# What a garbage collector sees through SuspendThread + GetThreadContext.
# Measured 2026-09-22 on winoracle (x64), 200 suspends per thread:
#   x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc -O1 -nostdlib -e probe_main -o p.exe \
#       tools/oracle_probe/suspend_context_probe.c -lkernel32
spinning  in_regs=0xc8 via_stack=0x0  MISSING=0x0 rsp_outside=0x0 api_fail=0x0
blocked   in_regs=0x0  via_stack=0xc8 MISSING=0x0 rsp_outside=0x0 api_fail=0x0
#
# Windows stops a thread wherever it is. The spinning thread's callee-saved
# magic is always in its registers; the blocked thread's callee saved it to
# the stack. MISSING is the column that matters: a GC scanning registers and
# stack never loses the value.
#
# Vitreo before 2026-09-22: the probe HUNG. SuspendThread waits (no timeout)
# for the target to park at a checkpoint, and a hot guest loop never reaches
# one -- both dispatch loops chain JIT blocks in an inner do/while that only
# leaves on cold blocks, thunks or stale code. The hang dump showed the target
# at suspend_depth=1 with its counter still climbing.
#
# Vitreo after: spinning in_regs=0xc8, blocked in_regs=0xc8 (not via_stack:
# Vitreo's host thunks do not clobber callee-saved registers), MISSING=0 both.
